Q. output of this code?
console.log("1");
setTimeout(() => console.log("2"), 0);
Promise.resolve()
    .then(() => console.log("3"))
    .then(() => console.log("4"));
queueMicrotask(() => console.log("5"));
console.log("6");

A. 1 6 3 5 4 2

4 does not immediately follow 3. The second .then() is queued as a new microtask 
  only after the first .then() finishes, 
  so the already-queued queueMicrotask() callback runs first

